&#x201C;I&#x2019;ve never done anything like this,&#x201D; Parker Posey says. She has certainly, over her singular 35-year screen career, sat down with journalists plenty, and likely on this very couch at the Chateau Marmont, where she&#x2019;s been staying over a busy weekend of events in Los Angeles. But our meeting has come on the heels of a dizzying press run for Posey, one that feels as much about her entire life onscreen as it is about her fresh projects that are ripe for promotion &#x2014; most significantly, her small but vivid role in Martin McDonagh &#x2019;s new Oscar-bound film, Wild Horse Nine . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I don&#x2019;t really have a reference point to this because I just got a publicist a few years ago,&#x201D; Posey says, between sips of her grapefruit juice. While the sustained exposure &#x2014; the periods of talking about oneself, really &#x2014; could seem daunting, you sense quickly that Posey approaches it like she does anything else. She excitedly orders olives and almonds and crudit&#xE9; for our lounge table. She happily ignores our time limit, even if she&#x2019;ll have to hail an Uber across town to meet some friends for lunch. She makes strong, direct eye contact, constantly shifting between my questions and her own curiosity about the person sitting before her. &#x201C;I bet we have friends in common,&#x201D; she says at one point. Related Stories TV 'My Favorite Murder' HBO Series Sets December Premiere Lifestyle John Malkovich Sets West End Return With Rosalind Eleazar in 'History'

There&#x2019;s nobody like Parker Posey, and this has been true for a long time across movies and TV. It&#x2019;s why she remains so synonymous with the great American indie-film run of the &#x2018;90s, why she can now both go viral with a single scream of a line &#x2014; see recent HBO examples in The Staircase and, of course, The White Lotus &#x2014; and still imbue the dialogue with surprising, heartfelt depth. And it&#x2019;s perhaps why, as Posey finally, really puts herself out there, there&#x2019;s a lot of love coming her way. You&#x2019;ll see it in the thrill of her pulling out a title at random in the Criterion Closet, selecting Ghost World , and cheering, &#x201C;I love this movie &#x2014; yay!&#x201D; Or in the warmth of her reviving her old bond with CBS Sunday Mornings correspondent Mo Rocca, as they quote Katharine Hepburn back and forth, grinning ear to ear. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;You&#x2019;re 15 again, at North Carolina School of the Arts with your gay bestie &#x2014; well, we didn&#x2019;t say that [term] then,&#x201D; Posey says of being interviewed by Rocca for that plum segment. &#x201C;It was so meaningful to me. Because you&#x2019;re always going to feel the same &#x2014; you'll just keep getting older. And it's true, I do still feel the same. I feel like that person, excited to be at NCSA with Maurice.&#x201D;

